 "low_power_caveat": "The >=1e-2 filter removes 85-92% of split_rows per step (most recipes live in the miscalibrated tail by sheer diversity, not because the calibrated range is empty), and within_target_fe_ols additionally drops any target with <2 surviving rows (its demeaned contribution is exactly 0). n_obs_in_fe_fit / n_targets_calibrated_with_ge2_obs above are the ACTUAL regression sample per step, smaller than n_rows_calibrated -- as low as 36 obs over 12 targets for S1. Read any sign flip in this calibrated-range fit as suggestive, not as statistically equivalent in power to the full-range result."
